<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Min Saw Mon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1380–1433</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Narameikhla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Min Saw Mon was the last king of the Launggyet period of Arakan and the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mrauk-u">Mrauk U</a> kingdom. Driven into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> by forces of the Ava kingdom in 1406, he regained his throne in 1429 with an army from the Bengal Sultanate. In 1430 he founded a new capital at Mrauk U, which remained the seat of Arakanese kings until 1785.</p></div>
